{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And he begot a son.</b> It is not written 'and he begot et Noah,' as it writes concerning the others, because from him the world was rebuilt — for the entire world was destroyed, and he and his sons remained. Another interpretation: Methuselah advised Lamech not to give him a name, because the men of the generation were sorcerers and would cast a spell upon him if they knew his name."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:03.460714709Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}